<article class="container info-page"><div class="eyebrow">FREEMCP / INFORMATION</div><h1>About FreeMCP</h1><p class="intro">Learn about FreeMCP, an independent community-driven directory of open-source MCP servers.</p><div class="info-content"><h2>Our mission</h2><p>FreeMCP helps developers discover open-source Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers and explore integrations for AI assistants. The registry brings project descriptions, source links, and available setup guidance into one place.</p><h2>How the registry works</h2><p>Community members can <a href="/submit/">suggest a public GitHub repository</a>. Submissions are reviewed before publication; inclusion is not a security audit, endorsement, or guarantee that a server will work in every environment.</p><h2>Independent and community-driven</h2><p>FreeMCP is an independent project maintained by <a href="https://github.com/strbbrn">strbbrn</a>. Some placements may be sponsored; promotional content is separate from the underlying server listings.</p><h2>Get involved</h2><p>Explore <a href="/servers/">the directory</a>, suggest a server, or <a href="https://github.com/strbbrn/freemcp-registry/issues">report an issue on GitHub</a>.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
